# Git guesses text-vs-binary by looking for NUL bytes. A PDF has none, so it
# is guessed as text and gets line-ending conversion on checkout -- which
# shifts every byte offset in its xref table and corrupts the file. The
# marker PDF's geometry is what the distance calibration is built on, so mark
# these explicitly rather than relying on the guess.
*.pdf   binary
*.npz   binary
*.zip   binary
*.ckpt  binary
*.bin   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary
